      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early industrialists floated lumber down the Saginaw River to mills, amassing fortunes that built the city’s first factories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_City%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city’s skyline is punctuated by four historic bridges—Liberty, Veterans Memorial, Independence, and Lafayette Avenue—crossing the Saginaw River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_City%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Industrial Brownhoist, founded in Bay City, pioneered railroad wrecking and wharf cranes that became standard gear worldwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        22,
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
